content:
The public Playground proves semantic construction without exposing the Agentic Ontology implementation.

Permitted

Display titles and public URLs for allow-listed public documents;

semantic concepts, relationships, state, and public citations;

Agent learning events, knowledge revisions, and generation receipts;

clearly labelled mock cognitive-package identity, state, and surface summaries.

Blocked

source code, code snippets, internal symbols, and call implementation;

repository file paths, line numbers, byte locations, or local absolute paths;

Git commits, branches, history, or source-tree details;

source maps, credentials, Secrets, or private URLs.

Build gate

The generator rejects dangerous fields and any Agent graph-query payload. The static-site checker scans generated JSON, HTML, JavaScript, CSS, and the file list. A forbidden field, absolute path, source map, or unsafe reference fails the build and stops deployment.
